('a84c26aa-7263-46ad-b934-462d4faa1cc4', 'The Empire Prequel 2', 'Bronze Rain', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire Prequel', '2.0', 'When the wells begin failing, Seyra of Black Reed trusts measurements more than promises. But as the desert shifts and water rises where it should not, she discovers that an ancient system beneath the sand is beginning to work again, threatening the fragile balance of survival.', '<p class="font_8">Bronze Rain</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Book Two of The Empire Prequel</strong></p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>The wells are failing. The desert is opening. And beneath the sand, something ancient is beginning to work again.</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">Seyra of Black Reed trusts measurements more than promises.</p>
<p class="font_8">When her family’s well drops below every known mark, she does what generations before her have done: count the depth, limit the draw, record the change, and keep people alive.</p>
<p class="font_8">Then the water rises.</p>
<p class="font_8">Without rain.</p>
<p class="font_8">Soon, buried stone appears beneath the dunes. Bronze-lined openings breathe cold air. Old roads emerge from the sand. Ancient structures begin revealing systems no living engineer fully understands.</p>
<p class="font_8">The discovery draws everyone.</p>
<p class="font_8">Gao engineers want to measure it.</p>
<p class="font_8">White Stag officials want to control it.</p>
<p class="font_8">Merchants see opportunity.</p>
<p class="font_8">Laborers see food.</p>
<p class="font_8">Black Reed families see outsiders building roads, camps, regulations, and authority on top of water their people have depended on for generations.</p>
<p class="font_8">Nobody begins with conquest in mind.</p>
<p class="font_8">That does not mean conquest cannot happen.</p>
<p class="font_8">As excavation expands, competent administration makes the project stronger. More workers arrive. More grain is distributed. More storage is built. More rules are written. Every new success becomes another reason not to stop.</p>
<p class="font_8">Seyra keeps asking the question officials dislike most:</p>
<p class="font_8">What happens when the system works exactly as intended, but the ground beneath it does not?</p>
<p class="font_8">Local records contradict official maps. Wells recover at different rates. Ancient structures shift. Dragons alter their routes. Pressure builds beneath the basin.</p>
<p class="font_8">Then the sky begins throwing metal.</p>
<p class="font_8">Hot bronze falls through rain and ash. Roofs collapse. Floodwater cuts evacuation routes apart. Official signs point people toward roads that no longer exist.</p>
<p class="font_8">And survival depends on the knowledge that never made it onto the government map.</p>
<p class="font_8">When the disaster becomes known as <strong>Bronze Rain</strong>, the fight changes.</p>
<p class="font_8">Now everyone needs a cause.</p>
<p class="font_8">A mistake.</p>
<p class="font_8">A saboteur.</p>
<p class="font_8">Someone whose name can fit beneath the catastrophe.</p>
<p class="font_8">But Seyra has dates.</p>
<p class="font_8">Witnesses.</p>
<p class="font_8">Water marks.</p>
<p class="font_8">Her father’s records.</p>
<p class="font_8">And a chronology that refuses to become the story powerful people need.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Bronze Rain</strong> is Book Two of <em>The Empire Prequel</em>, continuing the six-book story of how ancient technology, emergency rule, public works, political authority, and perfectly reasonable decisions begin building the world that will one day become <em>The Empire</em>.</p>
<p class="font_8">For readers who enjoy political epic fantasy, lost civilizations, ancient machinery, dragons, engineering disasters, survival, competing records, institutional power, family, dry humor, and characters forced to choose between what is useful and what is true.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>The ruins were buried for centuries.<br>
It takes only one generation to decide they belong to the state.</strong></p>', '497', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-08-01T04:00:00Z', '9798174960343', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK2S1927', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK2S1927', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('a8ea201a-aa35-48f3-9396-3d4c1b23a968', 'The Hollow Kingdom 6', 'Queen Below', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Hollow Kingdom', '6.0', 'At Northwatch, Tressa Vale helps establish the First House, where claims must be heard, the dead counted, and the living cannot be turned into vessels for old power. But as buried vaults awaken and a child begins answering for everyone, the new refuge faces a deeper threat.', '<p class="font_8">**The First House has opened. The vaults are waking. And beneath the Crown, a child has been answering for everyone.**<br>
<br>
Tressa Vale has done what the Crown never intended.<br>
<br>
At Northwatch, in the snow and blood of the Outer Mark, she has helped found the First House: a place where claims must be heard, the dead must be counted, and the living cannot be turned into vessels for old power.<br>
<br>
It should be a beginning.<br>
<br>
Instead, it becomes a breach.<br>
<br>
Beneath Crownmark, hidden vaults begin to open. Face plates wake. Silver masks rise. Records unfold themselves. Stored voices call from the dark. Every mechanism reveals another layer of what the Crown buried under words like order, relief, continuity, and mercy.<br>
<br>
Then the Gentleman is named.<br>
<br>
Thomas Arlen was once a man before hunger learned his handwriting. His office has stood beyond the chain, patient and polished, waiting for old debts to become useful again. But even he is not the deepest danger.<br>
<br>
Because another voice speaks from below.<br>
<br>
A child’s voice.<br>
<br>
The Inner Answer.<br>
<br>
For years, something beneath Crownmark has answered for queens, courts, and offices that preferred silence over truth. Now the child beneath the throne is awake, frightened, and being opened from the other side.<br>
<br>
Tressa must hold the First House together before it collapses under the weight of every hidden crime at once. Garran Holt stands beside her, burned nearly to ash but still refusing to leave. Mara fights for bodies that law tried to erase. Lysa writes through grief. Voss faces the wreckage of his own house. And every answer they uncover pulls them closer to the one truth the old kingdom never wanted spoken:<br>
<br>
No throne can be holy if a child was made to sit beneath it.<br>
<br>
**No Queen Below** is Book Six of **The Hollow Kingdom**, a dark romantasy series of haunted law, ancient bells, buried children, dangerous roads, gothic mystery, fierce found family, sharp banter, and a slow-burn love tested by every secret under the Crown.</p>', '292', 'Dark Romance / Gothic / Romantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-22T04:00:00Z', '9798183774566', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CJ6WN3', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CJ6WN3', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '31.99', '21.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('ad2fcba2-2a24-4ff7-b14c-b7261aa88a5d', 'Fugate', 'The Blood of Troublesome Creek', 'R.E. Smith', '', '', 'Sixteen-year-old Elias Fugate has the blue-tinged skin of his Kentucky family line, a mark that draws stares and suspicion. In Troublesome Creek, he searches for answers about his heritage, but the truth behind the blue bloodline proves more dangerous than local explanations suggest.', 'In the hills of Kentucky, some bloodlines do not fade. They wait. Sixteen-year-old Elias Fugate has always known he is different. His skin carries the strange blue cast of his family line, a mark that makes neighbors stare and churchgoers look away. In Troublesome Creek, everyone has an explanation, but nobody has the truth. When Elias asks why there are no other blue children his age, the answers turn dangerous. His father dodges the past, his grandfather keeps records that should have been burned, and the elders watch him like something promised has come due. The deeper Elias digs, the more he understands that the blue is not just a color. It is an inheritance. Inspired by the real legend of the Blue People of Kentucky, this is a dark Appalachian gothic novel of family secrets, buried sins, mountain folklore, and one boy’s fight to learn what his bloodline has hidden for generations.', '435', 'Horror / Appalachian Gothic', 'Available', '2026-06-10T04:00:00Z', '9798180746238', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H4RHQNPY', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H4RHQNPY', '', 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '17.68', '11.51', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('ad8e6fa2-9a02-45fa-b585-51bf4800dcc8', 'The Bone Crown', 'The Hollow King Saga', 'R.E. Smith', '', '', 'When Garran Vale finds a cow gutted and marked with a message, he realizes the warnings about King’s Cairn were never just stories. A black piece of bone draws his grandson Bram toward something awakened beneath the hill, and an old danger begins reaching into the family’s life.', 'When Garran Vale finds one of his cows gutted in the rain and carved with a message meant for him, he knows the old warnings about King’s Cairn were never just stories. Something under the hill has awakened, and it has taken an interest in his grandson, Bram. A black piece of bone washed from the earth after a storm seems like treasure to Bram, but to the thing beneath King’s Cairn, it is the first tooth of a broken crown. The Vale family is hunted by old magic, dead things, faceless men, drowned bells, false kings, and the buried will of the Hollow King. Garran is no king, only an old soldier, farmer, widower, and stubborn man with too many regrets. But when the dark reaches for his family, he stands in the way. A grim fantasy of family, sacrifice, old grief, and buried evil.', '500', 'Fantasy / Grim Fantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-01T04:00:00Z', '9798199477512', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H3JTNGCS', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H3JTNGCS', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '21.42', '13.67', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('b45135f2-4c92-49e6-9586-fbe615b26f10', 'The Hollow Kingdom 10', 'Last Treaty', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Hollow Kingdom', '10.0', 'Tressa Vale has survived impossible roads, buried claims, dead roads, and the Crown’s attempts to erase the truth. Now the roads have answered, the dragons have stood, and every old power must face the Last Treaty, the reckoning that will determine what kind of kingdom remains.', '<p class="font_8">**The roads have answered. The dead have been counted. The dragons have stood. Now every old power must face the Last Treaty.**<br>
<br>
Tressa Vale has survived the wrong road to Bellharrow, the waking throne, the First Road, the songless dead, the Outside Claim, the Witness Tree, Sanctuary, the Unrecorded Road, and the Season Wound.<br>
<br>
She has measured what should not move, named what the Crown wanted buried, and helped build a First House where witness matters more than power.<br>
<br>
Now Barrowgate comes for her.<br>
<br>
The old center of Crown Works measure has not forgotten how to command roads, cages, records, bells, children, and bodies. It still believes a wound can be named, seized, transported, and closed. It still believes usefulness is ownership.<br>
<br>
It is wrong.<br>
<br>
When Barrowgate sends a child turned into a bell mouth, the final war begins without banners. Valehurst must scatter records, hide children, protect witnesses, and hold long enough for the deeper road to open. Beneath the old bridge, Tressa, Holt, Mara, Branoc, and the others enter Hollow Edge, where Crown roads cannot command and the last treaty begins to take shape.<br>
<br>
But no treaty can survive if it repeats the old crime.<br>
<br>
The Crown cannot rule below. The Hollow cannot own the living. The dragons cannot remain weather engines. The dead cannot become offices. Children cannot be proof. Bodies cannot be payment. Measure cannot become ownership. And Tressa Vale cannot be turned into the map that saves everyone else.<br>
<br>
With Holt’s fire nearly spent and every ally carrying wounds of their own, Tressa must face Lock Seven, Barrowgate’s hidden records, the Empty Crown Record, and the final question waiting beneath every road in the Hollow Kingdom:<br>
<br>
Can a kingdom be saved without giving it a ruler to devour?<br>
<br>
**The Last Treaty** is the final book in **The Hollow Kingdom**, a dark romantasy series of dangerous roads, ancient bells, buried law, fierce witness, dragon-bound seasons, found family, gothic mystery, sharp-tongued allies, and a love strong enough to refuse every throne that asks for blood.</p>', '395', 'Dark Romance / Gothic / Romantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-22T04:00:00Z', '9798183800623', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CPVF8G', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CPVF8G', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '31.99', '21.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('b9eb21fc-da8d-4503-ad9a-0ed1daac8c62', 'The Hollow Kingdom 7', 'Counted Dead', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Hollow Kingdom', '7.0', 'The First House has survived its first night, but danger remains. At Northwatch, Tressa Vale helps create a place where the dead can be counted and the living can refuse to be used, until a bitten apple, a haunted well, and a bloodless white room threaten the fragile hope taking root.', '<p class="font_8">**A bitten apple. A haunted well. A white room where no one is allowed to bleed.**<br>
<br>
The First House has survived its first night.<br>
<br>
That does not mean it is safe.<br>
<br>
Tressa Vale has helped build a place where the dead can be counted and the living can refuse use. At Northwatch, witnesses gather under snow, law, hunger, grief, and the stubborn hope that truth can become more than a wound.<br>
<br>
Then a bitten apple appears on the eastern road.<br>
<br>
Inside it waits a map.<br>
<br>
The trail leads to the Well Road, where Bessa Dinn’s voice rises from the dark and points them toward Sanctuary. A name that should mean safety becomes something far worse: white gloves, polished halls, quiet bells, and mercy sharpened into control. In Sanctuary, pain is hidden, grief is cleaned, and children are altered until the living can look away more comfortably.<br>
<br>
Bessa is still alive.<br>
<br>
But not whole.<br>
<br>
Garran Holt’s fire, Mara’s body-law, Branoc’s transport cunning, and Tressa’s chain are pushed into a rescue where every hallway has learned to sound gentle while doing harm. Getting Bessa out is only the first fight.<br>
<br>
Because Sanctuary has patrons.<br>
<br>
They come to Northwatch with dogs, armed retainers, sealed claims, and a white-wrapped wagon that screams before anyone inside it can speak. The child within is called Little Grief, and his name, body, voice, and pain have all been divided for other people’s comfort.<br>
<br>
Now the First House must hold a hearing under siege.<br>
<br>
No forced return. No sealed claim. No patient as property. No grief made clean for the living.<br>
<br>
But the small door is still waiting.<br>
<br>
Before third dawn, the Hollow Kingdom demands one who chooses, one who paid, and an answer full enough to pour.<br>
<br>
**The Counted Dead** is Book Seven of **The Hollow Kingdom**, a dark romantasy series of haunted roads, ancient bells, gothic mystery, dangerous mercy, fierce found family, slow-burn devotion, and a kingdom where even the dead are finally given standing.</p>', '304', 'Dark Romance / Gothic / Romantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-22T04:00:00Z', '9798183782868', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CC6NR9', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CC6NR9', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '31.99', '21.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('bb2eec8a-8c50-4742-9617-db6c19f872ab', 'The Hollow Kingdom 5', 'Witness Tree', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Hollow Kingdom', '5.0', 'Tressa Vale has followed impossible roads through buried bells, stolen memories, false claims, and Crown offices that turned people into useful things. Now the road leads north toward Northwatch, where the dead gather and the first true witness house may be born in blood.', '<p class="font_8">**The dead are gathering. The road is counting. And the first true witness house may be born in blood.**<br>
<br>
Tressa Vale has followed impossible roads through buried bells, false claims, stolen memories, and Crown offices that turned people into useful things.<br>
<br>
Now the road leads north.<br>
<br>
Northwatch waits beyond the Green Mile, the King’s Cup, and Kingless Ford, each place returning another piece of what the kingdom tried to take. Edric Voss is being restored one stolen fragment at a time. Oran’s old wound is opening into something no royal court can safely name. Children, ghosts, claimants, and broken witnesses are beginning to gather around Tressa’s chain.<br>
<br>
The Crown wants order.<br>
<br>
The Gentleman wants payment.<br>
<br>
The Hollow Kingdom wants answer.<br>
<br>
At the Outer Mark, beneath first snow, Tressa and Holt must help found what should have existed long ago: a First House where claims are heard one at a time, bodies are not vessels, and the dead are not converted into convenient silence.<br>
<br>
But witness is dangerous.<br>
<br>
Every name entered creates standing. Every truth spoken threatens old power. And when Crown Relief arrives from the storm wearing silver closed-eye masks and carrying bell-metal spears, the First House will have to prove it can stand before it has even finished being written.<br>
<br>
Garran Holt’s fire can hold back some monsters. Tressa’s chain can answer some claims. Neither can make the cost gentle.<br>
<br>
Because the Witness Tree has taken root.<br>
<br>
And once it begins to write, no crown, creditor, office, or kingless road can pretend the dead were never there.<br>
<br>
**The Witness Tree** is Book Five of **The Hollow Kingdom**, a dark romantasy series of haunted roads, ancient bells, dangerous law, sharp-tongued allies, slow-burn devotion, gothic mystery, and a kingdom where even grief demands standing.</p>', '404', 'Dark Romance / Gothic / Romantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-22T04:00:00Z', '9798183770858', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6D12ZDN', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6D12ZDN', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '31.99', '21.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('bb92175d-4f98-47ef-b8de-80560edc7041', 'The Empire Prequel 3', 'The First Chain', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire Prequel', '3.0', 'After the disaster at First House, the ancient network beneath the roads can no longer be dismissed as a buried curiosity. Stations respond to heat, pressure, vibration, and unknown signals, and the effort to prevent another catastrophe begins creating the first chain of control.', '<p class="font_8">The First Chain</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Book Three of The Empire Prequel</strong></p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>They survived Bronze Rain. Now everyone wants to make sure it can never happen again.</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">That is how the first chain begins.</p>
<p class="font_8">After the disaster at First House, the ancient network beneath the roads can no longer be dismissed as buried curiosity. Stations respond to heat, pressure, vibration, and signals nobody fully understands. Roads once thought ordinary begin revealing older purposes.</p>
<p class="font_8">At Western Lamp, water runs uphill.</p>
<p class="font_8">A bronze throat hums beneath the ground.</p>
<p class="font_8">A child notices patterns the instruments miss.</p>
<p class="font_8">And every new answer creates three more questions.</p>
<p class="font_8">The governments of White Stag and Gao begin connecting what Bronze Rain exposed. Engineers test buried stations. Officials classify routes. Maps are standardized. Access is restricted. Local knowledge becomes strategic information.</p>
<p class="font_8">The work is careful.</p>
<p class="font_8">Measured.</p>
<p class="font_8">Often responsible.</p>
<p class="font_8">Which makes it even harder to see where caution ends and control begins.</p>
<p class="font_8">Because the old roads do not belong only to governments.</p>
<p class="font_8">They cross farms, wells, caravan routes, pastures, and communities whose families knew the land long before officials began calling it infrastructure. A goat path can become strategic overnight simply because a map says so.</p>
<p class="font_8">Then there is Ash Neck.</p>
<p class="font_8">The dragon is not attacking cities. She is following something.</p>
<p class="font_8">Warm seams.</p>
<p class="font_8">Old vents.</p>
<p class="font_8">Buried lines.</p>
<p class="font_8">Whenever crews activate the ancient network, her routes change with it.</p>
<p class="font_8">Selen wants to understand why.</p>
<p class="font_8">Tuvan wants to make sure she cannot reach a working station.</p>
<p class="font_8">Both have evidence.</p>
<p class="font_8">Neither has certainty.</p>
<p class="font_8">The argument becomes brutally simple:</p>
<p class="font_8">Move the road.</p>
<p class="font_8">Or move the dragon.</p>
<p class="font_8">When another required test draws Ash Neck into a staffed corridor, the state chooses capture.</p>
<p class="font_8">Not because she is declared evil.</p>
<p class="font_8">Not because anyone proves she is hostile.</p>
<p class="font_8">Because she has become unpredictable in a place the government has decided must function.</p>
<p class="font_8">The operation succeeds.</p>
<p class="font_8">Men die.</p>
<p class="font_8">Horses die.</p>
<p class="font_8">Ash Neck survives in chains.</p>
<p class="font_8">And once she is inside the walls, captivity immediately begins acquiring procedures, titles, ledgers, handlers, medical rules, custody agreements, and permanent records.</p>
<p class="font_8">By the third morning, someone has already written the word <strong>permanent</strong>.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>The First Chain</strong> is Book Three of <em>The Empire Prequel</em>, continuing the six-book story of how ancient infrastructure, public safety, political necessity, and fear slowly become institutions powerful enough to outlive the emergencies that created them.</p>
<p class="font_8">For readers who enjoy political epic fantasy, dragons treated as living creatures rather than symbols, ancient technology, engineering, law, contested land, institutional power, family, dry humor, and moral choices where every side has enough truth to be dangerous.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>A chain does not become permanent when the lock closes.<br>
It becomes permanent when everyone learns to live around it.</strong></p>', '509', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-09-01T04:00:00Z', '9798174963788', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK2S6GHM', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK2S6GHM', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('bc19e765-80f2-4980-9fa7-a7a84828b82c', 'Crown of Cinders 1', 'The City Owes Blood', 'R.E. Smith', 'Crown of Cinders', '1.0', 'Sable Rook knows that in Crownfall, innocence is only a debt not yet collected. As the Synod tightens its grip and turns law into scripture, Rook is drawn into a struggle where names can kill, bargains shape power, and survival means understanding who truly controls the city.', '<p class="font_8">In Crown of Cinders: The City Owes Blood, power doesn’t march in daylight—it signs its name and lets the bells do the killing.<br>
<br>
Sable Rook has survived long enough to know one rule: in this city, innocence is just debt you haven’t been forced to pay yet. When the Synod begins tightening its grip—turning law into scripture and scripture into a noose—Rook is pulled into a struggle where names matter more than swords, and a single ledger can topple districts like rotten beams.<br>
<br>
But something older is waking beneath the stone. A voice that shouldn’t exist rides the seams of doors. A crown doesn’t simply sit on a head—it chooses, it hungers, and it opens what was meant to stay shut. As allies fracture, enemies smile from behind clean titles, and the city’s “order” starts to smell like ash, Rook must decide what to save and what to burn… even if the fire takes her with it.<br>
<br>
This is adult epic fantasy—grim, fast, and razor-edged—where politics and blood run in the same channels, magic has rules that bite, and every victory comes stamped with a cost.<br>
<br>
Because the city owes blood.<br>
And sooner or later, it collects.</p>', '473', 'Epic / Dark Fantasy / Sword & Sorcery', 'Available', '2026-01-03T05:00:00Z', '9798242441378', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GDW54C2B', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GDW54C2B', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '25.92', '15.05', '<p>To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('bd7e1e03-a486-435f-8092-74a9a9ec5f5f', 'The Empire 7', 'Border Fire', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire', '7.0', 'Nine months after Blood Charter, the north has become more stable and attractive to people fleeing oppressive governments. But as refugees arrive and strange changes unsettle the land, leaders must decide how to protect their borders without allowing protection to become another form of tyranny.', '<p class="font_8">Border Fire</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Book Seven of The Empire</strong></p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>They built a country people wanted to enter. Then the border asked what protection was allowed to become.</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">Nine months after <em>Blood Charter</em>, the north is more stable, more lawful, and more attractive to people fleeing governments that are neither.</p>
<p class="font_8">Then the refugees begin arriving.</p>
<p class="font_8">At Daran Well, warm water rises where cold water should be. Animals refuse old roads. Bronze hums beneath human hands. Smoke spreads across the southern horizon, and villages empty north before anyone understands whether they are running from civil war, something beneath the earth, or both.</p>
<p class="font_8">At the frontier, Qulan faces the problem every successful state eventually creates:</p>
<p class="font_8">People want in.</p>
<p class="font_8">Families arrive hungry, wounded, armed, frightened, and carrying laws, debts, loyalties, grudges, and claims from the country behind them. The Charter can give water without citizenship. It can give medical care without allegiance. It can protect a camp without annexing the land beneath it.</p>
<p class="font_8">The harder question is what happens when violence follows the refugees to the line.</p>
<p class="font_8">Ashar March does not ask to be conquered.</p>
<p class="font_8">It asks for help.</p>
<p class="font_8">That distinction becomes the center of the war.</p>
<p class="font_8">As local councils petition for association, the Charter must decide the difference between asylum, residence, representation, military protection, and membership. Qulan is eventually invited across the old frontier under a narrow defense mandate, only to discover how quickly temporary protection becomes checkpoints, searches, food control, road closures, armed patrols, and foreign troops who are still there tomorrow.</p>
<p class="font_8">Xu and Mei Ren confront the same problem from the coast as relief ships and armed escorts risk becoming something larger. Ilyara fights to write limits strong enough to survive fear. Samira Veyran, a former Saffron tax clerk, enters Charter protection with her children and discovers that a functioning system can be both humane and unsettling. Rakhim Saren must decide whether loyalty to his country requires obedience to men destroying it.</p>
<p class="font_8">And beneath every political argument, something older is changing.</p>
<p class="font_8">Water heats without cause. Bronze vibrates. Compasses fail. Dragons alter their routes. Old roads behave strangely.</p>
<p class="font_8">The evidence is real.</p>
<p class="font_8">The explanation is not.</p>
<p class="font_8">By the time war reaches Kestrel Gate, Mazar Quay, and Three Arches, the question is no longer whether the Charter can win.</p>
<p class="font_8">It is whether it can help another country survive without quietly becoming its ruler.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Border Fire</strong> is Book Seven of <em>The Empire</em>, opening the final trilogy of the completed nine-book adult epic fantasy saga.</p>
<p class="font_8">For readers who enjoy political fantasy, refugee crises, military intervention, border conflict, constitutional tension, morally complicated warfare, dragons, found family, romance, occupation pressure, and fantasy where doing the right thing does not automatically give anyone the right to rule.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>A border can keep an army out.<br>
It cannot keep history buried.</strong></p>', '688', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-04-01T04:00:00Z', '9798174588950', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJYY5W18', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJYY5W18', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('c1686916-19dc-474a-8c36-d8496f880af3', 'The Empire 1', 'Rising Sun', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire', '1.0', 'A summit at Red Gate becomes the opening move in a conspiracy involving Jade forces, the White Stag, the Temür, and crimes inherited from a generation that thought the past could stay buried. Arslan returns to a fortress crowded with old loyalties and political dangers that may reshape the dawn of a new Empire.', '<p class="font_8">Rising Sun</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Book One of The Empire</strong></p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Two suns rise. Only one can own the dawn.</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">Red Gate was supposed to be a summit.</p>
<p class="font_8">Instead, it becomes the opening move in a conspiracy involving Jade forces, the White Stag, the Temür, and crimes inherited from a generation that believed the past could remain buried.</p>
<p class="font_8">Arslan returns to the fortress and finds Yuclan waiting there, along with old loyalties, old wounds, and a political trap built from the sins of their parents. When Shen Ru attempts to expose the operation, he is destroyed. Temür settlements come under attack. Survivors scatter. And Arslan’s private losses become the spark of a rebellion he never intended to lead.</p>
<p class="font_8">At the Jade court, Emperor Xu discovers that his own authority has been used without his consent. He can still choose the throne.</p>
<p class="font_8">Or Yuclan.</p>
<p class="font_8">He chooses.</p>
<p class="font_8">The decision fractures the balance of power.</p>
<p class="font_8">A dragon is freed. Red Gate breaks. Arslan escapes north with survivors and an army, while Xu watches the same dawn from the opposite side of the Wall.</p>
<p class="font_8">What begins as a conspiracy becomes a living war.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Rising Sun</strong> launches <em>The Empire</em>, a completed nine-book adult epic fantasy saga of rebellion, loyalty, political power, ancient forces, inherited guilt, war, love, and the terrible cost of deciding what kind of world should rise from the ruins of the old one.</p>
<p class="font_8">For readers who enjoy sprawling political fantasy, morally complicated characters, ancient mysteries, warfare with consequences, shifting alliances, and empires built as much by choices as by swords.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Every empire begins with a decision.<br>
This one begins at dawn.</strong></p>', '541', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Available', '2026-10-01T04:00:00Z', '9798194913411', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HGKS68DJ', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HGKS68DJ', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '32.0', '17.0', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('c28f8e9f-855c-4ae4-8d1e-f0f43ce20e22', 'Wolves of Tiber 3', 'Shadow Kings', 'R.E. Smith', 'Wolves of Tiber', '3.0', 'Rome has survived the purge, but its new regime must now keep the city from tearing itself apart. Strange changes stir beneath the streets, while Aurelio and the leaders of the new order face restless neighborhoods, dangerous old secrets, and the burden of building a future from the ruins.', '<p class="font_8">Rome survived the purge.<br>
Now it must survive what comes after.<br>
Something is changing beneath the city—down in the buried veins of old Rome, where stone remembers names that were never meant to be spoken again. The new regime holds the gates and the councils, but the streets are restless, the rooftops are tense, and the ruin belt is louder than ever.<br>
<strong>Aurelio</strong> carries the weight of a founder—he must keep Rome from tearing itself apart.<br>
<strong>Remo</strong> carries a mark that won’t cool, a hunger that won’t stay quiet, and a rage that won’t be ruled.<br>
As secrets rise and old bargains snap tight, the brothers are pushed toward an ending neither of them can escape. Enemies can be killed. Monsters can be hunted. Even a city can be rebuilt.<br>
But a bloodline at war with itself?<br>
That becomes legend—or a grave.<br>
In the final volume of <em>Wolves of Tiber</em>, the external threat is defeated… and the internal fracture hardens into something permanent.<br>
Because in Rome, power doesn’t just demand sacrifice.<br>
It chooses who will make it.</p>', '476', 'Genre Fiction / Horror / Dark Fantasy / Epic / Historical', 'Available', '2026-01-01T05:00:00Z', '9798279246342', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GB53VRHR', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GB53VRHR', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '20.94', '13.19', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('c406fe0d-a99d-421b-be55-c9683fc475b7', 'Children of the First Blood', 'Book Zero of The Lilith Covenant', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Lilith Covenant', '', 'Before Blood of Eden and Castle Noctivar, Lilith and Baal establish the first blood covenant beneath an ancient Bronze Age sanctuary in Mesopotamia. Their children hunt by night, and blood becomes the key to doors and powers that will shape the vampire houses for generations.', '<p class="font_8">Before Blood of Eden, before Castle Noctivar, before the vampire houses learned to hide behind silk, crowns, and old money, there was the First House Below.</p>
<p class="font_8">Beneath an ancient sanctuary in Bronze Age Mesopotamia, Lilith and Baal have built the first blood covenant. Their children hunt by night, dragging the innocent through reed marshes and canal roads to feed the bowls below. Child blood opens doors. Adult blood sustains. Royal blood empowers. And beneath the earth, the Blood Father waits while the Blood Mother sings.</p>
<p class="font_8">Naru was raised in that darkness.</p>
<p class="font_8">To the blood-children, he is nothing but a drudge, a quiet servant who scrubs bronze bowls after the rites and keeps his eyes down. But Naru carries a secret even he does not fully understand. He is the forbidden son of Lamashtu, born of vampire hunger and human blood, hidden beneath Lilith’s law and Baal’s command.</p>
<p class="font_8">When one stolen child escapes through a crack in the lower shrine, the old war wakes. Enki, Gilgamesh, and the human Scorpion Guard begin to close around the hidden sanctuary. Naru is forced to choose between the family that made him and the children they feed upon.</p>
<p class="font_8">But Lilith’s covenant is older than mercy, Baal cannot be buried like a man, and victory may only teach the darkness how to survive.</p>
<p class="font_8">Children of the First Blood is Book Zero of The Lilith Covenant and the ancient origin story behind Blood of Eden. Brutal, mythic, and blood-soaked, it tells how the first vampire covenant was broken, how the first warning was written, and how one forbidden son learned that blood can open doors, but choice decides what walks through them.</p>', '415', 'Dark Fantasy / Horror › Vampires / Occult & Supernatural', 'Available', '2026-07-03T04:00:00Z', '9798185179635', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H7FH3K6D', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H7FH3K6D', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '22.0', '17.0', '<p>To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('de6bb098-6772-4c5e-9eff-ed8191a96c95', 'The Empire 9', 'The Final Road', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire', '9.0', 'Across Tartaria, ancient barriers rise, roads obey dead authority marks, and water systems fail as buried mechanisms begin enforcing rules no living government understands. The roads are closing by memory, forcing a final choice between saving the system and saving the people who depend on it.', '<p class="font_8">The Final Road<br>
<br>
Book Nine of The Empire<br>
<br>
They can save the system. They can save the people. They cannot guarantee both.<br>
<br>
The roads are closing.<br>
<br>
Not by decree.<br>
<br>
By memory.<br>
<br>
Across Tartaria, ancient barriers rise from buried stone. Roads sort wagons according to dead authority marks. Water systems fail. Mountains fracture. Dragons abandon old ranges. Long-buried mechanisms begin enforcing classifications no living government recognizes and no living ruler authorized.<br>
<br>
The Deep Meridian is failing.<br>
<br>
And for the first time, everyone knows enough to understand what that means.<br>
<br>
The same buried network capable of regulating water, stabilizing roads, controlling pressure, and holding a continent together also carries the machinery of classification and command that earlier empires learned to weaponize. It is not evil. It is not a god. It is not a mind waiting to be defeated.<br>
<br>
It is infrastructure.<br>
<br>
And it still works.<br>
<br>
That makes the choice worse.<br>
<br>
As routes collapse and refugee columns begin moving, a new emergency office is proposed: First Command.<br>
<br>
One authority.<br>
<br>
One chain of communication.<br>
<br>
One system capable of coordinating armies, engineers, transport, food, roads, and evacuation across the entire crisis.<br>
<br>
It saves time.<br>
<br>
It reduces losses.<br>
<br>
It works.<br>
<br>
And Qulan refuses to take it.<br>
<br>
Then Khasar is offered something even more dangerous.<br>
<br>
Permanent synchronization.<br>
<br>
His unusual compatibility with the Deep Meridian could allow one living person to coordinate the network strongly enough to stabilize much of physical Tartaria. Roads could reopen. Water could move. Pressure failures could be contained.<br>
<br>
Cities might survive.<br>
<br>
Millions might survive.<br>
<br>
All it would require is rebuilding the central point of control the entire series has spent eight books learning to distrust.<br>
<br>
And putting a fifteen-year-old boy inside it.<br>
<br>
While politicians argue over First Command and engineers fight to understand a system collapsing beneath their feet, the final objective changes.<br>
<br>
Not victory.<br>
<br>
Evacuation.<br>
<br>
Qulan and Ochen hold the northern roads long enough for civilians to move. Xu and Mei Ren turn the Office toward a maritime evacuation involving ports, hospitals, families, food, and hundreds of thousands of displaced people. Lan Su must destroy water systems she spent years learning to save. Huan watches mountains empty and dragons flee. Rakhim opens the southern road into Ashar while fighting men determined to close it.<br>
<br>
At Red Gate, the archives are triaged.<br>
<br>
Some records are saved.<br>
<br>
Some are deliberately destroyed.<br>
<br>
And some disagreements are preserved because history without dissent would only become another weapon.<br>
<br>
The final war spreads across cavalry roads, harbors, rivers, mountains, and the buried heart of Red Gate.<br>
<br>
But there is no throne left to win.<br>
<br>
Only time.<br>
<br>
Time to move the children.<br>
<br>
Time to move the wounded.<br>
<br>
Time to move the records.<br>
<br>
Time to open one last road before the system that built an empire tears the land apart beneath it.<br>
<br>
The last question of The Empire is not who deserves to rule.<br>
<br>
It is whether a civilization can choose to die rather than become the thing it once fought to destroy.<br>
<br>
The Final Road is Book Nine and the concluding novel of The Empire, completing the nine-book adult epic fantasy saga.<br>
<br>
For readers who enjoy political fantasy, civilization-scale catastrophe, military evacuation, ancient technology, constitutional conflict, dragons, family, sacrifice, morally impossible choices, and finales where saving the world may require letting the old one end.<br>
<br>
The empire does not survive.<br>
The people do.</p>', '715', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-06-01T04:00:00Z', '9798174621145', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK22QR4P', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK22QR4P', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('df238d7a-c180-4781-a3c1-6915424dbe2f', 'The Empire 8', 'Ash Meridian', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire', '8.0', 'When a mountain opens, it reveals not a god or buried king but ancient infrastructure: galleries, bronze mechanisms, water regulators, roads, and sealed interfaces. As the ground itself begins issuing orders, the people above must confront the systems that have quietly shaped their world for generations.', '<p class="font_8">Ash Meridian</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Book Eight of The Empire</strong></p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>They promised to leave when asked. Then the ground began giving orders.</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">The mountain has opened.</p>
<p class="font_8">What waits inside is not a god, a prophecy, or a buried king.</p>
<p class="font_8">It is infrastructure.</p>
<p class="font_8">Ancient galleries, bronze mechanisms, water regulators, road systems, sealed chambers, and buried interfaces stretch beneath a continent whose people have spent generations fighting over the ruins above them. The deeper investigators go, the harder one truth becomes to ignore:</p>
<p class="font_8">The old world was not merely built on top of these systems.</p>
<p class="font_8">It was built around them.</p>
<p class="font_8">At the same time, the political victory of <em>Border Fire</em> begins creating a quieter danger.</p>
<p class="font_8">Ashar March asked the Charter for protection. Now Charter soldiers guard roads, Charter engineers keep water moving, Charter ships carry food, Charter courts settle disputes, and Charter institutions have become woven into daily life.</p>
<p class="font_8">Temporary help is becoming permanent dependence.</p>
<p class="font_8">And dependence has a way of looking remarkably similar to occupation when everyone involved is competent enough.</p>
<p class="font_8">Qulan must prove that an army invited onto foreign soil can actually leave it. Xu and Mei Ren confront systems whose usefulness makes withdrawal painful. Ilyara and Neris fight over the difference between consent written into law and consent that remains meaningful after people depend on what they are being asked to surrender.</p>
<p class="font_8">Khasar, now old enough to understand what people see when they look at him, wants an ordinary life of horses, roads, tools, and work.</p>
<p class="font_8">The ancient systems have other measurements.</p>
<p class="font_8">As water failures spread and buried regulators begin responding across distant regions, scholars give the connected network a name:</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>The Deep Meridian.</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">It can regulate water.</p>
<p class="font_8">Open roads.</p>
<p class="font_8">Stabilize failing systems.</p>
<p class="font_8">Move food faster.</p>
<p class="font_8">Perhaps even prevent catastrophe.</p>
<p class="font_8">But the same machinery once classified people, controlled routes, recognized authority, and decided who was permitted to pass.</p>
<p class="font_8">When one ancient regulator is deliberately reactivated to save lives, it works.</p>
<p class="font_8">That is the problem.</p>
<p class="font_8">Soon old roads begin sorting travelers. Forgotten barriers rise. Supply routes open for some and close for others according to rules no living government wrote. The temptation is no longer theoretical.</p>
<p class="font_8">Perfect infrastructure has returned.</p>
<p class="font_8">So has the authority buried inside it.</p>
<p class="font_8">Meanwhile, Ashar prepares to decide its own future.</p>
<p class="font_8">Remain permanently inside the Charter.</p>
<p class="font_8">Or leave.</p>
<p class="font_8">The Charter has always claimed association is voluntary.</p>
<p class="font_8">Now it must prove that promise while enemies gather, supply systems strain, and withdrawal makes everyone less safe.</p>
<p class="font_8">By the time the last checkpoints come down, one border has been removed by human choice.</p>
<p class="font_8">Another rises from beneath the earth.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Ash Meridian</strong> is Book Eight of <em>The Empire</em>, the middle novel of the final trilogy in the completed nine-book adult epic fantasy saga.</p>
<p class="font_8">For readers who enjoy political fantasy, ancient technology, buried civilizations, military occupation, constitutional conflict, archaeological mystery, dragons, morally complicated institutions, family, romance, and stories where the most dangerous machine is the one that genuinely works.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>They learned how to live without an empire.<br>
Now the earth remembers how to build one.</strong></p>', '697', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-05-01T04:00:00Z', '9798174592728', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJZY8HVY', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJZY8HVY', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('e23818ad-39ee-41df-9d11-2c8889c6c4ed', 'INDEPENDENCE', 'A Lifetime at Sea', 'R.E. Smith', '', '', 'In the final months of World War II, the heavy cruiser USS Independence crosses the Pacific with secret cargo, unfinished repairs, and nearly twelve hundred men aboard. When the ship dies in twelve minutes, the survivors must carry the consequences of what happened long after the wreck.', 'The ship took twelve minutes to die. The men left behind would spend a lifetime carrying what happened next. In the final months of World War II, the heavy cruiser USS Independence is sent across the Pacific with secret cargo, unfinished repairs, and nearly twelve hundred men aboard. Commander Brendan O’Rourke knows the ship is being pushed too hard. Captain Nathaniel Rusk knows the route is dangerous. Nineteen-year-old Ensign Sammy Kerr only knows he has finally reached the war and is desperate to prove he belongs there. Then two torpedoes strike. The Independence disappears beneath the Pacific, leaving her survivors scattered across a black sea with little water, few rafts, worsening wounds, and no sign that anyone is searching for them. As hope fades, O’Rourke gives himself one order: remember every name. When rescue finally comes, the Navy finds fewer men than expected and more truth than it wants. Escort requests were ignored, reports mishandled, and warnings vanished into clean offices and careful language. Independence: A Lifetime at Sea is a World War II naval tragedy about courage, brotherhood, guilt, sacrifice, and the burden carried home by those the sea allowed to live.', '777', 'Historical Fiction / World War II', 'Available', '2026-07-19T04:00:00Z', '9798186991106', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H8MWH53K', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H8MWH53K', '', 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '27.0', '17.0', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('e57cd530-aa1f-445b-9a20-0a0beeb7dd2f', 'The Hollow Kingdom 2', 'First Road', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Hollow Kingdom', '2.0', 'Tressa Vale survived the buried throne beneath Crownmark, but the danger has only begun. The floor rings and ancient roads answer from across the kingdom, drawing her toward forgotten laws, broken bells, and the truth behind a system that measures people as if they were property.', '<p class="font_8">**The throne is empty. The roads are waking. And the Crown has not finished measuring the dead.**<br>
Tressa Vale survived the buried throne beneath Crownmark, but survival did not end the danger. It only proved the Hollow Kingdom was real.<br>
Now the floor rings beneath her feet.<br>
The old roads are answering from every direction. Bellharrow. Greyveil. Applecross. Crownmark. Places bound by buried law, broken bells, forgotten claims, and debts the living never paid properly. The Crown wants order. Royal Survey wants control. The Hollow Kingdom wants witness.<br>
Tressa is caught between all three.<br>
Marked by the throne and bound to the brass chain of her office, she has become something the capital cannot ignore. Garran Holt, the burned and stubborn Warden at her side, is the one man who understands how dangerous that makes her. He is also becoming harder to keep at a safe distance, which would be inconvenient even if the kingdom were not actively trying to rearrange itself under their boots.<br>
Then Royal Survey reveals the fifth measure.<br>
Obedience.<br>
It is older than law, cleaner than murder, and far more useful to people who prefer their crimes official. In the capital, roads can be made straight, bells can command, and the dead can be filed away until no one has to remember who gave the order.<br>
Tressa, Holt, Mara, and Voss must enter the machinery of Crown power before the first road wakes fully and every claim below the kingdom is forced into one obedient line.<br>
But the Hollow Kingdom was never built for one ruler.<br>
And the first road does not open for cowards, kings, or liars.<br>
**The First Road** is Book Two of **The Hollow Kingdom**, a dark romantasy series filled with dangerous magic, gothic courts, ancient bells, buried law, sharp banter, slow-burn heat, and a kingdom that refuses to stay dead.</p>', '469', 'Dark Romance / Gothic / Romantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-22T04:00:00Z', '9798183644609', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CQZTF3', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CQZTF3', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '31.99', '21.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('e9f83e83-3491-4cb2-95a2-4a6f2182d6db', 'RUADH RÌGH', 'Ash and Oaths', 'R.E. Smith', '', '', 'Thirteen-year-old Ruadh Rìgh MacSweyn grows up in the painted highlands beyond Rome’s walls, where his father rules by hard law and harsher consequences. As Rome advances through fire, hunger, and betrayal, the young heir must prove he has the nerve and judgment to lead his people.', '<p class="font_8">Rome doesn’t conquer the north with honor. It conquers it with fire, hunger, and men willing to sell their neighbors.<br>
<br>
Ruadh Rìgh MacSweyn is thirteen when the world starts sharpening around him. In the painted highlands beyond the empire’s walls, his father—Angus Mór, chief of the MacSweyn túath—rules by hard law and harder consequence. Ruadh is the heir… if he can prove he has the nerve to lead, the stomach to spill blood, and the spine to survive the kind of betrayal that comes smiling.<br>
<br>
Then Ruadh meets **Sìne**—a girl from a neighboring tribe he’s not supposed to touch, let alone love. Their courtship begins in secret at the Highland games and burns into an oath the clans never approved. It also paints a target on them both.<br>
<br>
Because rivals are everywhere.<br>
<br>
Neighboring chiefs and their sons want the MacSweyn seat and will do anything—poison, lies, hostage-work—to claim it. **Beli of the River Mouth** plays friend while feeding Rome the gaps in the north. And Roman scouts circle the forests like wolves, baffled by warriors who don’t march in lines, who vanish into trees, who strike at night and melt into the land as if the land itself fights back.<br>
<br>
As Rome pushes deeper into Caledonian territory, tribal politics turn brutal. Love becomes leverage. Loyalty becomes a blade you either hold… or feel in your ribs. The pressure peaks at **Mons Graupius**, where Ruadh marches into his first true battle and learns the ugliest truth of war:<br>
<br>
Sometimes the worst slaughter happens behind the lines.<br>
<br>
By the time the smoke clears, Ruadh is eighteen—crowned by loss, hunted by rivals, and forced to lead what’s left of his people into exile. With Dunvegan burning behind them and the western sea ahead, the survivors gamble everything on hired ships and a new home on **Benbecula**.<br>
<br>
It isn’t a happy ending. It’s a survived ending.<br>
<br>
**RUADH RÌGH: ASH AND OATHS** is a gritty, adult historical epic—part romance, part blood-soaked survival—where the north fights an empire, clans fight each other, and a young Mor learns that a crown isn’t gold…<br>
<br>
…it’s ash held together by oaths.<br>
<br>
**Perfect for readers who love:**<br>
<br>
* Braveheart-meets-Game-of-Thrones grit (adult, not rated-X)<br>
* Political betrayal, tribal warfare, and hard-won leadership<br>
* Dangerous romance in a world where vows have consequences<br>
* Roman-era invasion pressure and Caledonian resistance at the edge of history</p>', '525', 'War & Military / Ancient & Classical / General', 'Available', '2025-12-23T05:00:00Z', '9798241009241', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GC4D3WDR', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GC4D3WDR', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '19.48', '11.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('ebefefe3-9a82-4fc1-8c63-b25677fd254e', 'The Empire 5', 'Iron Levy', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire', '5.0', 'Eight months after Salt Crown, the famine has eased, grain is moving, and roads are open, but the emergency institutions remain. Relief offices and armies have discovered how useful they are, raising a dangerous question: will the systems built for survival ever surrender the power they gained?', '<p class="font_8">Iron Levy</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Book Five of The Empire</strong></p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>The famine taught governments what survival cost. Peace teaches them how many soldiers that cost can buy.</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">The emergency is ending.</p>
<p class="font_8">The armies are not.</p>
<p class="font_8">Eight months after <em>Salt Crown</em>, the grain is moving again, the roads are open, and the worst of the famine has eased. But the institutions created to survive it have discovered something dangerous:</p>
<p class="font_8">They are useful.</p>
<p class="font_8">Relief offices now control ships, payrolls, repair yards, armed escorts, debt powers, and contracts. Families that once signed for food now sign for wages. Villages trade service for security. Young men and women discover that a uniform can pay burial debts, buy seed, provide medicine, and keep a household alive.</p>
<p class="font_8">No one calls it conscription.</p>
<p class="font_8">Not yet.</p>
<p class="font_8">Orri knowingly signs a three-year service contract because the money can save his family. He understands that soldiers fight and sailors drown.</p>
<p class="font_8">What he does not yet understand is how quickly the purpose of an army can change after the signature is dry.</p>
<p class="font_8">Across the continent, the machinery of defense begins hardening into something permanent. Xu must decide whether emergency military authority can be dismantled without leaving millions exposed. Qulan commands forces created for defense while civilian governments fear the soldiers they now depend upon. Boro fights a system capable of turning deserters into criminals and poverty into recruitment. Arslan watches political disagreements acquire uniforms, ships, weapons, and payrolls.</p>
<p class="font_8">Every argument now has armed men standing behind it.</p>
<p class="font_8">Then the violence begins.</p>
<p class="font_8">Blue Reef.</p>
<p class="font_8">East Chain.</p>
<p class="font_8">Iron Yard.</p>
<p class="font_8">Greywater.</p>
<p class="font_8">Broken Chain.</p>
<p class="font_8">Each battle, riot, fire, assassination, and military order makes the next emergency easier to justify. The same societies that learned to price famine are learning to price soldiers.</p>
<p class="font_8">And when Arslan is murdered at Red Gate, grief does what no law has managed to do.</p>
<p class="font_8">It mobilizes armies.</p>
<p class="font_8">Forces that were created to protect free people begin marching toward one another, each carrying lawful orders, legitimate grievances, dead friends, and enough iron to turn a political crisis into continental war.</p>
<p class="font_8">The final question is no longer whether military service is good or evil.</p>
<p class="font_8">It is harder than that.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>If a person freely agrees to one dangerous purpose, how much can the state change that purpose before consent becomes obedience?</strong></p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>Iron Levy</strong> is Book Five of <em>The Empire</em>, the second novel in the series’ second trilogy and part of the completed nine-book adult epic fantasy saga.</p>
<p class="font_8">For readers who enjoy military fantasy, political intrigue, naval warfare, morally complicated alliances, soldiers caught between duty and conscience, dragons, romance, assassination, mass battles, and fantasy worlds where laws can become weapons long before anyone draws a sword.</p>
<p class="font_8"><strong>The army is already here.<br>
The question is who gets to point it.</strong></p>', '728', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-02-01T05:00:00Z', '9798174539938', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK12GKWV', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HK12GKWV', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('f3082fb8-935f-4c04-ac55-a770da8a0246', 'The Hollow Kingdom 8', 'Unrecorded Road', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Hollow Kingdom', '8.0', 'After the First House survives its first siege, Tressa Vale continues the work of witness at Northwatch, where every answer reveals another buried room beneath the kingdom’s clean records. Unrecorded roads, strange shoes, and a broken winter crown point toward a truth the Crown refuses to admit.', '<p class="font_8">**A hidden road waits beyond the door. No map records it. No Crown office admits it exists.**<br>
<br>
The First House has survived its first siege.<br>
<br>
That should mean the worst is behind them.<br>
<br>
It is not.<br>
<br>
At Northwatch, the work of witness continues, and every answer digs up another buried room beneath the kingdom’s clean records. Empty white Sanctuary shoes appear in the snow, each pair requesting review. Winter’s broken crown wakes in seven dangerous shards. A blue bird key points toward a quiet nursery room beneath Greyveil. And old ledgers begin to reveal the shape of a system larger than any one office.<br>
<br>
Children were not only taken.<br>
<br>
They were traded.<br>
<br>
Crown, Hollow, Sanctuary, Voss, Wardenry, Vale, Road, and Outside all left marks on the stolen, the hidden, and the misnamed. Tressa Vale has built a house where truth can stand, but truth is beginning to arrive faster than any ledger can hold it.<br>
<br>
Then Crownmark opens another wound.<br>
<br>
At the East Archive stair, a woman hidden beneath gray cloth is revealed: Maereth Ysmark, a royal living return classified as dead and used when the Inner Answer child could not answer. Her existence threatens Crown continuity, Queen Ysabet’s rule, and the old machinery that kept inconvenient bloodlines locked away from daylight.<br>
<br>
Garran Holt stands beside Tressa through every new breach, every old bell, every map that tries to correct itself around her. Their bond has become stronger than caution and more dangerous than either can name. But love does not make the road safe. It only gives them another reason to keep standing.<br>
<br>
Because beyond the small Northwatch door waits something older.<br>
<br>
An unrecorded road.<br>
<br>
Stakes wrapped in cloth line the dark ground. Some cloth bears names. Some bears teeth marks. Some bears nothing at all. And far between the black trees, something carries a lantern and speaks as if it has waited a very long time.<br>
<br>
The First House has learned to read.<br>
<br>
Now the road that was never written is ready to answer.<br>
<br>
**The Unrecorded Road** is Book Eight of **The Hollow Kingdom**, a dark romantasy series of haunted roads, buried children, ancient bells, fierce witness, gothic mystery, slow-burn devotion, sharp-tongued allies, and a kingdom whose hidden records are finally opening.</p>', '354', 'Dark Romance / Gothic / Romantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-22T04:00:00Z', '9798183792768', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CYMGSF', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CYMGSF', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '31.99', '21.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('f40cadf7-3c1c-481a-99f8-edcdc6c81908', 'The Hollow Kingdom 3', 'Songless Line', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Hollow Kingdom', '3.0', 'When a black northern road knocks three times, Tressa Vale and the Hollow Kingdom must face a new mystery. Northwatch has gone dark beyond the mapped world, and a village without song must find its voice before the lower bell rings again.', '<p class="font_8">**A road knocks from the north. A queen is offered a crown. A village without song must find its voice before the lower bell rings again.**<br>
<br>
Tressa Vale has survived impossible roads, buried thrones, and Crown offices that measured people like property.<br>
<br>
She has not survived rest.<br>
<br>
When the black northern road knocks three times, the Hollow Kingdom turns toward it. Northwatch has gone dark beyond the mapped world, and every awakened road seems to understand what the Crown refuses to admit: something old is waiting there.<br>
<br>
But the north is not the only danger.<br>
<br>
In Crownmark, courtiers and churchmen try to force Queen Ysabet back into the shape of old power. They call it stability. They call it duty. Tressa has learned to distrust any offer that comes wrapped in clean cloth and expects someone else to bleed quietly beneath it.<br>
<br>
Garran Holt remains at her side, burned, dangerous, and increasingly impossible to keep at a sensible distance. His fire can stop old things from taking her. It cannot make the choices easier. Not when the kingdom keeps tying witness, love, law, and survival into the same hard knot.<br>
<br>
Then Bellharrow answers again.<br>
<br>
Beneath the village waits the lower bell, and it does not ring for kings. It rings for broken crossings, unfinished names, dead voices, and a village that forgot how to sing when singing mattered most.<br>
<br>
To stop the north from swallowing what they have barely begun to save, Tressa and Holt must face the cost of silence, the danger of crowns, and the truth that some roads do not open until people learn to answer together.<br>
<br>
**The Songless Line** is Book Three of **The Hollow Kingdom**, a dark romantasy series of waking roads, ancient bells, dangerous courts, haunted villages, slow-burn heat, sharp-tongued allies, and love forged under impossible law.**</p>', '451', 'Dark Romance / Gothic / Romantasy', 'Available', '2026-06-22T04:00:00Z', '9798183756210', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CNH857', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H6CNH857', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '31.99', '21.99', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('f723bfcb-d421-4852-8bfc-1537ad5870cc', 'Crowns of Blood 2', 'The Black Roar', 'R.E. Smith', 'Crowns of Blood', '2.0', 'Ten years after Kethria falls, the scars of war still smoke across Aeldrith. Kingdoms rebuild and crowns are reforged, but something ancient moves in the frozen reaches beyond the known lands, threatening to turn the fragile peace into another devastating conflict.', '<p class="font_8"><strong>Crowns of Blood – Book II</strong></p>
<p class="font_8">The fire that saved them may yet burn the world.</p>
<p class="font_8">Ten years after the fall of Kethria, the scars of war still smoke across Aeldrith. Kingdoms rebuild. Crowns are reforged. Oaths are spoken in quieter halls.</p>
<p class="font_8">But in the frozen reaches beyond the known lands, something ancient has begun to move.</p>
<p class="font_8">They come out of the frost and timberline like walking avalanches. Towering. Fur-matted. Red-eyed in the dark. The Urskarn were once whispers told to frighten children.</p>
<p class="font_8">Now they are real.</p>
<p class="font_8">And they are hungry.</p>
<p class="font_8">Villages vanish overnight. Farmlands burn. Stone walls splinter beneath claw and rage. Steel slows them. Arrows anger them. Only fire truly kills them—and even then, not easily.</p>
<p class="font_8">Vaelric stands at the center of it all. No longer a child of ruin, but not yet the ruler the realm demands. With dragons at his call and enemies circling from within and without, he must decide what kind of power he is willing to become.</p>
<p class="font_8">Because commanding dragons is one thing.</p>
<p class="font_8">Commanding what they burn is another.</p>
<p class="font_8">As blue flame meets red, as black fire coils with gold, the skies over Aeldrith blaze with a fury not seen since the first war. Fields turn to ash. Armies break. Old alliances fracture under the weight of fear.</p>
<p class="font_8">The Urskarn do not negotiate.</p>
<p class="font_8">They do not retreat.</p>
<p class="font_8">And when they roar, mountains answer.</p>
<p class="font_8"><em>The Black Roar</em> is a sweeping epic of dragons, siege and sacrifice, of a realm forced to choose between mercy and survival. Brutal, cinematic, and relentless, this second installment in the <strong>Crowns of Blood</strong> series raises the stakes higher than ever before.</p>
<p class="font_8">In a world rebuilt by flame…</p>
<p class="font_8">What happens when the fire answers back?</p>', '433', 'Epic / Dark Fantasy / Sword & Sorcery', 'Available', '2026-04-09T04:00:00Z', '9798249881696', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FTG7RWH3', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FTG7RWH3', '', 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, '22.4', '14.71', '<p>To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '', ''),
('43ab168c-ce03-4117-9b2c-ae2dded64c2b', 'Ashes of Haverhill', 'The Tale of Hannah Duston', 'R.E. Smith', '', '', 'In the brutal spring of 1697, a raid devastates Haverhill and changes one family’s fate. This historical reimagining of Hannah Duston’s story explores survival, faith, and the brutal realities of life on the colonial frontier.', '<p class="font_8">In the brutal spring of 1697, the town of Haverhill is torn apart by a raid that shatters one family and forges an unlikely legend. <em>Ashes of Haverhill</em> reimagines the true story of Hannah Duston — a Puritan woman thrust into the darkest corners of frontier life — and follows her unflinching fight to survive loss, captivity, and the wilderness itself.</p>
<p class="font_8">From the terror of the raid to the harrowing escape across the Merrimack River, Hannah’s journey is one of grit, tragedy, and impossible choices. Returning home brings no peace. She finds her children gone, her husband wounded, and her life reduced to embers. Yet from that devastation she rebuilds: tending her broken homestead, grieving the family she lost, and ultimately discovering an unexpected second chance with Daniel Cheney — a turn that would shape generations to come.</p>
<p class="font_8">Told through the warm, lyrical voice of a modern-day storyteller, the novel weaves past and present as a Florida grandfather shares Hannah’s saga with his grandchildren by the campfire. What begins as a tale of survival becomes a meditation on legacy, resilience, and the quiet courage of ordinary people confronting extraordinary times.</p>
<p class="font_8">Blending historical detail with narrative heart, <em>Ashes of Haverhill</em> brings new life to one of New England’s most controversial heroines, culminating in a powerful reflection on what it means to endure, rebuild, and rise again.</p>
<p class="font_8">For readers who love frontier history, strong women, and stories carried across generations, this is Hannah Duston as you’ve never seen her — not just a figure of legend, but a woman of flesh, fire, and indomitable will.</p>', '83', 'Colonial Period / Cultural Heritage / Historical', 'Available', '2025-11-24T05:00:00Z', '9798275802283', 'eBook; Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G3PJ5324', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G3PJ5324', 'https://play.google.com/store/audiobooks/details/R_E_Smith_Ashes_of_Haverhill_The_Story_of_Hannah_D?id=AQAAAEBGUBkQTM', 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, '13.33', '6.6', '<p>To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p class="font_8">To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', 'ashes-of-haverhill', ''),
('97819b72-d9ab-40c6-83f3-08a5a1af8599', 'The Empire 4', 'Salt Crown', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire', '4.0', 'Fourteen months after Black Dawn, freedom has survived, but barely. Broken infrastructure, failing reservoirs, divided currencies, migrating dragons, and poor harvests leave the new governments struggling to rebuild, while a powerful new offer to finance recovery comes with its own dangers.', '<p class="font_8">Salt Crown<br>
<br>
Book Four of The Empire<br>
<br>
The first trilogy broke the chain. Now someone has arrived offering to finance the repair.<br>
<br>
Fourteen months after Black Dawn, freedom has survived.<br>
<br>
Barely.<br>
<br>
The old Wall network is broken. Roads fail. Reservoirs no longer answer one another. Currencies divide. Dragons migrate. Harvests falter. And every government born from the collapse of the old order discovers the same ugly truth:<br>
<br>
Principle does not fill a granary.<br>
<br>
Then the white sails appear.<br>
<br>
The Nine Harbors Compact comes carrying what everyone desperately needs: grain, salt, ships, quarantine medicine, standardized measures, credit, and protection for the roads between starving cities. Its relief works. People eat. Trade resumes. Disease is contained. Lives are saved.<br>
<br>
But every rescue arrives with terms.<br>
<br>
A signature here. A harbor right there. A labor agreement. A debt guarantee. A marriage clause. An emergency lease that will outlive the emergency.<br>
<br>
And when hunger makes refusal deadly, consent becomes a dangerous word.<br>
<br>
Xu must keep an empire fed without rebuilding the tyranny he helped destroy. Arslan watches free settlements discover that independence can still be purchased one contract at a time. Mei Ren and her infant daughter become targets of political bargains neither of them chose. Across the new governments, rulers, workers, merchants, soldiers, and families are forced to decide how much freedom they can afford before winter decides for them.<br>
<br>
The Compact is not an invading army.<br>
<br>
That would be easier.<br>
<br>
It is competent. Useful. Wealthy. Organized.<br>
<br>
And it can save lives.<br>
<br>
Its power grows through salt, grain, ships, insurance, debt, wages, harbor access, and contracts freely signed by people who may have no meaningful alternative. The crown in Salt Crown is no piece of gold. It is the name ordinary people begin giving to a system that can rule without ever sitting on a throne.<br>
<br>
As famine tightens its grip and a storm fleet pushes every alliance toward breaking, old enemies must cooperate again. But this time the question is not whether they can defeat a tyrant.<br>
<br>
It is whether free people can remain free when survival itself has a price.<br>
<br>
Salt Crown is Book Four of The Empire, beginning the second trilogy of the completed nine-book adult epic fantasy saga.<br>
<br>
For readers who enjoy political fantasy, economic warfare, morally complicated alliances, famine and survival, naval conflict, dragons, family, romance, shifting loyalties, and worlds where the most dangerous weapon may be a perfectly legal contract.<br>
<br>
A crown is not always worn.<br>
Sometimes it is built from salt.</p>', '480', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-01-01T05:00:00Z', '9798174536494', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJZGMBR5', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJZGMBR5', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', 'the-empire-4', ''),
('a25e02bb-b989-4ea0-bbbc-c9f48f145274', 'The Empire Prequel 6', 'The False Peace', 'R.E. Smith', 'The Empire Prequel', '6.0', 'Peace has arrived: wars are over, roads are open, and markets are full. Then Altana finds a goat recorded in an accounting ledger, revealing how a system that claims to be fair can quietly punish ordinary families and turn small administrative decisions into instruments of control.', '<p class="font_8">The False Peace<br>
<br>
Book Six of The Empire Prequel<br>
<br>
The wars are over. The roads are open. The markets are full. Peace has finally arrived.<br>
<br>
Then Altana finds a goat in an accounting ledger.<br>
<br>
A hill family failed to provide two men for a spring road crew. One son was sick. The other was away with sheep. The father was lame.<br>
<br>
The district took a goat.<br>
<br>
No soldiers beat anyone. No house burned. No one died.<br>
<br>
The road was cleared.<br>
<br>
Peace remained excellent.<br>
<br>
Months later, the goat appears beneath a harmless phrase:<br>
<br>
LOCAL BURDEN BALANCING.<br>
<br>
Altana begins looking closer.<br>
<br>
A charcoal family fined for missing transport duty.<br>
<br>
A river settlement charged after refusing storage seizure.<br>
<br>
A northern clan penalized for failing to provide escorts.<br>
<br>
Different governments.<br>
<br>
Different rules.<br>
<br>
The same pattern.<br>
<br>
Powerful houses negotiate before obligation.<br>
<br>
Weak communities discover the terms after refusal.<br>
<br>
Peace is reciprocal at the top and compulsory at the bottom.<br>
<br>
No council ever wrote a law saying:<br>
<br>
Hurt the weak to preserve peace.<br>
<br>
No one had to.<br>
<br>
One policy avoided burdens likely to provoke retaliation.<br>
<br>
Another shifted those burdens elsewhere.<br>
<br>
Another favored communities least able to resist.<br>
<br>
Each rule made sense alone.<br>
<br>
Together, they formed a machine with no single inventor.<br>
<br>
But Altana''s investigation uncovers something darker than unfair taxation.<br>
<br>
Old ledgers point toward private experiments involving ancient material.<br>
<br>
Fear.<br>
<br>
Blood.<br>
<br>
Human subjects.<br>
<br>
A note hidden inside a binding claims the mysterious pearl-like substance responds better after fear.<br>
<br>
The claim may be wrong.<br>
<br>
That does not make it harmless.<br>
<br>
Because people believed it enough to hurt others trying to prove it.<br>
<br>
The trail moves north.<br>
<br>
Records disappear into family property, government offices, merchant networks, and forgotten winter stores. Not every missing page is conspiracy. Sometimes history vanishes because someone gives a ledger to a brother and assumes winter will keep investigators away.<br>
<br>
Sometimes that is enough.<br>
<br>
Now Altana, Shen, Vahram, Orun, and the people who inherited generations of laws, compromises, and carefully preserved evidence must decide whether peace can be repaired without destroying the institutions holding it together.<br>
<br>
Because the system is not failing.<br>
<br>
That is the problem.<br>
<br>
It is working exactly as generations taught it to work.<br>
<br>
The False Peace is Book Six and the conclusion of The Empire Prequel, completing the story of how necessity became procedure, procedure became institution, and institution became the world inherited by Rising Sun.<br>
<br>
For readers who enjoy political epic fantasy, buried conspiracies, institutional power, ancient technology, legal intrigue, family legacies, investigative mysteries, dry humor, and stories where the final enemy is not a monster or a king, but a system everyone helped build.<br>
<br>
Peace did not become false because the fighting stopped.<br>
It became false when everyone agreed not to count who was paying for it.</p>', '384', 'Fantasy / Epic / Historical / Military ↗', 'Preorder / scheduled', '2027-12-01T05:00:00Z', '9798177506890', 'eBook (preorder); Paperback; Hardcover', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HL7GMSXJ', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HL7GMSXJ', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '', '', '<p class="font_8">To order a book directly, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, requested format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and your shipping address. Please include any special instructions. I will confirm availability, shipping cost, total price, and payment arrangements before the order is finalized. Do not send payment until the total is confirmed.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', '<p>To request a signed copy, email resmithauthor@gmail.com with the book title, format (paperback or hardcover), quantity, and the name or message you would like included, if any. Signed-copy prices are the listed paperback or hardcover price plus $2. Shipping is additional and will be confirmed with the total before payment. Please wait for confirmation of availability and total cost before sending payment.</p>', 'resmithauthor@gmail.com', 'the-empire-prequel-6', '');